 stroke via chlorotoxin-anchored, lexiscan-loaded nanoparticles. Nanomedicine 12, 1833&#8211;1842 (2016).</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5045320</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">27039220</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Haber AH &amp; Rothstein BE Radiosensitivity and rate of cell division: &#8220;law of Bergonie and Tribondeau&#8221;. Science 163, 1338&#8211;1339 (1969).</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">5765114</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Sorensen CS et al. The cell-cycle checkpoint kinase Chk1 is required for mammalian homologous recombination repair. Nat Cell Biol 7, 195&#8211;U121 (2005).</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">15665856</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Bernhard EJ et al. Inhibiting ras prenylation increases the radiosensitivity of human tumor cell lines with activating mutations of ras oncogenes. Cancer research 58, 1754&#8211;1761 (1998).</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">9563495</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Yang H et al. Radiosensitization of brain metastasis by targeting c-MET. Lab Invest 93, 344&#8211;353 (2013).</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">23381625</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Chen Y et al. EMMPRIN regulates tumor growth and metastasis by recruiting bone marrow-derived cells through paracrine signaling of SDF-1 and VEGF. Oncotarget 6, 32575&#8211;32585 (2015).</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC4741713</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">26416452</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Franken NA, Rodermond HM, Stap J, Haveman J &amp; van Bree C Clonogenic assay of cells in vitro. Nat Protoc 1, 2315&#8211;2319 (2006).</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">17406473</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference></ReferenceList></PubmedData></PubmedArticle